       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Dose:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults is 3,200 mg/day. This order is double that.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risk:** At this level the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events goes up a lot.\n\nCommon regimens are:\n- 400\u2013800 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours (maximum 3,200 mg/day) for pain or inflammation\n- 400 mg PO every 4\u20136 hours as needed for mild to moderate pain (maximum 2,400 mg/day is typical in practice)\n\nDid you mean 1600 mg per day in total, for example 400 mg four times daily? Or did you mean 800 mg four times daily, which is 3,200 mg/day? Tell me the dose you want and I'll enter it. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I would still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
